{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Tries\/Se","doc:\/\/Tries\/SE","doc:\/\/Tries\/SQ","doc:\/\/Tries\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/Tries\/SH","doc:\/\/Tries\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Tries\/ST","doc:\/\/Tries\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/trie"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are sequences of "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, stored as "},{"code":"[Symbol]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"Trie<Character>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holds words,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the same words scalar by scalar, "},{"code":"Trie<UInt8>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" byte strings. Lookup,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O("},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"σ","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") for a key of "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and at most "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" children per vertex. A trie answers the queries a hash set cannot: every key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a prefix, whether any key has one, and the longest key that is a prefix of a query."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the trie holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/PrefixView"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/init()","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/init(_:)"],